Task 1: Create and Configure Virtual Instances
1. Open VMware Workstation Pro 17
1. Start VMware Workstation Pro 17.
2. Open the existing Ubuntu 24.04.1 LTS virtual machine.
2. Clone Virtual Machines
1. Right-click the existing Ubuntu VM.
2. Select Manage → Clone.
3. Select Create a full clone.
4. Give the cloned VM a suitable name.
5. Repeat the process to create 2 or 3 additional VMs.
3. Power On the Cloned VMs
1. Right-click each cloned VM.
2. Select Power On.
3. Open the terminal inside each VM.
4. Install Apache Web Server
Perform the following steps inside each VM.
Update packages:
sudo apt update

Install Apache:
sudo apt install apache2 -y

Enable Apache:
sudo systemctl enable apache2

Check Apache status:
sudo systemctl status apache2

5. Customize the Apache Web Page
Open the Apache HTML file:
sudo nano /var/www/html/index.html

Modify the HTML page so that each VM has a unique page/message.
Save and exit:
Ctrl + O
Enter
Ctrl + X

6. Find the IP Address of Each VM
Run:
ifconfig
if it is not working - sudo apt install net-tools -y
Record the IP address of every VM.
Example:
VM1 → <VM1_IP>
VM2 → <VM2_IP>
VM3 → <VM3_IP>
